Title: Seat evidence recorded after gaze voids the review it records
Created: 2026-10-27
Author: Minh Ha-Duong

--- log ---
2026-10-27T08:23Z Minh Ha-Duong created
2026-10-27T09:21Z Minh-Ha-Duong note PR #1710 (ticket 1238): no seat reports in the range, verify-gate used review_evidence legacy and approved in round 1; the trap fires on partial evidence (some seats recorded, others no-report or stale), not on none

--- body ---
## Context
Since PR #1698 (ticket 1225), verify-gate requires per-seat review reports under `tickets/reviews/<base..head>/`, and a `no-report` placeholder does not count. Two failures follow, both hit by raid 1229:
- `/gaze` posts its result comment but writes no seat reports, so a gate on a REVIEWED head refuses for missing evidence (PR #1702 round 1 REROLL, PR #1699).
- Recording the reports afterwards adds commits under `tickets/reviews/`, which `BOOKKEEPING` in `scripts/merge-gate.py:81` does not list. `tier --since <reviewed head>` then answers `full`, so the act of recording evidence voids the review it records (PR #1702 round 2 ESCALATE; PR #1699 gate refusal). Both PRs landed only on the author's ruling.
A third, smaller trap: seat reports can carry absolute worktree paths, which `check-agnostic.sh` rejects in the merge-gate record (PR #1699, fixed by hand in 50f9301e).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] One ordering holds and is tested: either gaze records its own seat reports for the range it reviewed, before the gate, or the gate treats `tickets/reviews/` additions as bookkeeping for tier purposes (state which, and why the other was rejected: bookkeeping evidence must not skip the review it attests)
- [ ] A PR whose only post-review commits are its ticket close and its seat reports reaches verify-gate APPROVED with no author override (regression test on a fixture range)
- [ ] Seat reports never contain an absolute path: the recorder writes paths relative to the worktree, with a test
- [ ] `review_evidence.py record` does not block on stdin when run in the background

## Raid annotation (Imagine+Plan, 2026-10-27, wave 4)
- **Verdict: GO.** All four criteria survive on main (origin/main 66c57ab3). Nothing in 1225/1227/1248/1244 touched them.
- **Live today.** `scripts/merge-gate.py` `BOOKKEEPING = ("tickets/*.erg", "tickets/closed/*.erg", "STATE.md", "memory/")` (l.96 on main) has no `tickets/reviews/` entry, so `tier --since <reviewed head>` answers `full` after seat reports land. `skills/verify-gate/SKILL.md` l.378-387 ("No gate without a completed review") uses exactly that `tier --since` answer to accept a moved head. Inverse is already handled: `scripts/review_evidence.py exempt_paths` (l.202) takes plain added `100644` `*.md` files under `tickets/reviews/` out of the patch-id identity, so the seat table does not go stale; only the tier reading is wrong. Gaze still writes no seat reports (no `review_evidence.py record` in skills/gaze).
- **Ordering (criterion 1), recommended: gate-side.** Add the same shape as `exempt_paths` to the tier reading: pattern `tickets/reviews/*/*-*.md`. Why not gaze-records-first: gaze reviews a head and cannot commit onto the PR without moving it, so the commit after it is unavoidable; the exemption already exists for identity. Guard against "evidence skips the review it attests": only pure additions of non-executable `.md` count (the sneak-hook test, tests/test_review_evidence.py l.342, shows the mode check lives in `exempt_paths`); a modified or deleted report is `full`. This requires `changed_entries`/`tier_of` (merge-gate.py l.216-241) to see the status and mode, not just the path; check what it carries before choosing a bare pattern.
- **1245 effect: none on this ticket.** It keeps `BOOKKEEPING`, `is_bookkeeping`, `cmd_tier`; it deletes `effective`/`accepted_scopes` tier handling and `tiers`/`rerun` keys, so a record-content tier disappears but the `tier --since` gaze-freshness reading (this ticket's trap) stays. Do not sequence behind it, but rebase: both edit scripts/merge-gate.py (1236: constants + `tier_of`; 1245: `effective`, `accepted_scopes`, `cmd_run`, `load_config`, `cmd_plan`) and skills/merge/SKILL.md § Gating tiers.
- **1241 effect.** Gaze will mark `self-only` reviews and the reuse rule treats them as missing. If gaze becomes the recorder (criteria 1 alt), a `self-only` seat report must not be exempted as bookkeeping evidence of an independent review; the exemption should key on the report file shape, never on its verdict. Check 1241's wording lands first or leave the interface as file shape.
- **Criteria 3-4 (untouched by anyone).** Absolute paths: `check-agnostic.sh` rejects them in the record; `review_evidence.py record` writes `args.repo`-relative range dirs but report bodies come from stdin (cmd_record l.335); strip the worktree prefix in the recorder before writing. Stdin: `body = sys.stdin.read()` blocks when run detached; read only if `not sys.stdin.isatty()` and add `--body-file`. Tests in tests/test_review_evidence.py.
- **Risk.** Low. Fixture range for criterion 2 is a temp repo with reviewed head, then a commit adding `tickets/reviews/<r>/correctness-1.md` plus a ticket close; assert `tier --since` exits 0.
